<h2>What actually happens</h2>
<ul class="checks">
  <li>The app reads your public RSS feed, like any other player.</li>
  <li>The listener downloads the file straight <strong>from your server</strong>, and the download is counted on your side.</li>
  <li>We don't keep a copy, and there's no proxy, CDN of ours or storage of any kind in between.</li>
  <li>Ads your server inserts dynamically reach the listener exactly as your server sent them.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the processing does</h2>
<p>It evens out the volume between speakers, on the device, while someone listens. Your file doesn't change, and none of it is stored. In practice it's like a listener turning the volume knob themselves, except the app does it for them.</p>

<h2>If you'd rather not</h2>
<p>Send the show's name and feed address, and it will be removed from the app. We won't ask why and we won't set conditions.</p>
